```xml
<page type="text">
  <layout>One column of running text, full width. Running head "AD LECTOREM." at the top. Catchword at the lower right below the last line. No page number, no margin notes.</layout>
  <running_head>AD LECTOREM.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>uerius[?]</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <p cont="true">legisse, uel si legerit, perfunctorie legisse, uel denique non intellexisse uideatur. Sic artis medendi fundamenta ab eo nimium audacter,nec dicam imperitè coertutur[?], me-dicationis &amp; certissimæ summa affectur confusio. Iſtud quidem aduersus hos grauissimos authores fieri,nec pa-tronum[?] unum, qui oculum Fernelio reponeret inueniri sem-per,ut debui,uehementer dolui. At in nobilissima arte pro ueritate uanitatem haberi prudentissimis medendi legibus ſtolidam temeritatem ſubſtitui; denique pro arte periculum aſſumi, ita ægrè tuli, ut ab eo tempore nō cōquieuerim donec his meis exercitationibus, quaſi ſigno dato excitarem uel quoſdam ex multis, qui non Hippocratis, aut Galeni, ſed ueritatis ipſius patrocinium ſuſcipèrent. Hæc igitur nobis progymnaſmata fuerint, quæ ſint inſignis alicuius uictoriæ prænuntia, cuius gloriam aliis libentissimè concedo. Quicquid ſanè ago, eo ſine[?] ago, ut alijs ad maiora uiam planiorem faciam, eo animo ab omnibus, qui iſta legent acceptum iri confido. Equidem cum de ſcriptis meis nō magnopere laborare ſoleam, lateréq; ſemper concupiuerim, tamen hoc ſcriptum meum cupio, &amp; legi, &amp; ad exteros peruenire, ut extet aliquod teſtimonium amoris erga præclaros illos medicinæ authores mei. Ac ne quis, forte eorum, qui nimia facilitate, uel potiùs ſimplicitate in legendis aliorum ſcriptis decipi ſe patiantur, exiſtimet me uel contradicendi ſtudio, uel ambitiosa cupiditate ad hæc ſcribenda, impulſum uenisse, Deum immortalem teſtor nihil mihi tale in mentem incidisse, nihilq; uerius</p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Several words are uncertain and should be checked against the scan: "coertutur" (line 3, read as coërcentur[?]); "affectur" (line 4); "trouum" (line 6, read as unum); "pa-tronum[?]" (line 12, the line-end word is uncertain); "eo sine[?] ago" (line 16); "uerius" (catchword, printed as "ucrius"). The lines shown with a [?] are the places where my reading is least sure. The paragraph is one printed paragraph and continues from the previous page.</notes>
</page>
```